= Obtaining the Internship

I first heard about the Google internship pipeline from a friend who was
already interning at Google. She forwarded me the open requisition for the
European Software Engineering intern cohort and walked me through the
timeline, which was tighter than I had expected and several months earlier
than the comparable cycles at other companies. There was no formal referral
through the system — by the time I was ready to apply, the role I had my eye
on was already public — so I submitted my application through the Google
Careers portal in the normal way and went through the standard interview
loop: a recruiter screen, two coding interviews focused on data structures
and algorithmic reasoning, and a follow-up conversation in which a host
manager described the team and the project.

The team that picked me up was Web Performance, working specifically on
*Perfetto*, Google's open-source performance analysis stack. I received the
offer in late winter and joined as a *Software Engineering Intern* on the
2#super[nd] of June 2025. I remained with the team for the full thirteen
weeks of the internship, finishing on the 29#super[th] of August 2025.

